  "notes": "Source: official BCCC 'Surgical Technologist, AAS' program brochure/flyer (bccc.edu, 2024 edition) — 'Career Suggested Sequence of Courses' transcribed verbatim. The catalog program page (2024-2025, poid=1266, 'Program: Surgical Technologist, AAS') renders only the 'Suggested Sequence of Courses' heading with no table content (verified via direct fetch and the search index), so the official brochure is the authoritative term-by-term source. Prereq phase per brochure: PRE 100 (1cr), Biology Placement Exam 0cr (test out of BIO 101), Computer Literacy Exam 0cr (test out of CLT 100), ENG 101 (3cr), 'Modern Elementary Statistics or Precalculus I: College Algebra' MAT 107 or MAT 128 (3 or 4cr), SPE 101 (3cr) = 10-11cr. The two 0-credit exams are documented here, not as courses. MAT slot recorded at 3cr (MAT 107) to reconcile to the brochure's 64-credit lower bound (range 64-65 preserved here). Semester subtotals (13/11/5/13/12) + prereqs (10) = 64. Selective admission process; students must maintain a minimum 'C' in each SGT, AH, and science course. CAAHEP-accredited; graduates are eligible to sit for the certification exam given by the National Board of Surgical Technologists and Surgical Assistants. The SGT program is strictly a day program. Per-course prerequisites are not published on the program page; prereq lists are empty. [Coordinator correction 2026-10-01: total_credits set to 54 (= sum of sequenced course credits) per corpus convention (external_prereqs excluded from the sum; cf. ABAC plans); collector had recorded 64 including the prerequisite phase. The catalog's printed program total and the prerequisite phase remain documented above.]",
